**Review routing (operator decision, 2026-10-29):** the author, **Bybifok (GitHub: moust4ki)**, may run this PR's adversarial review himself, with a **Fable** sub-agent.

**Why it is allowed:**
- EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7 requires a cross-contributor review only for:
  - state-changing flows, sessions, auth, cookies and tokens;
  - security findings;
  - `HFRModels` public types and ADRs.
- This PR adds tests only, plus one CHANGELOG-LEGACY row. None of those cases applies.
- The rule that still applies is AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model. This PR was written by Opus 5.5, so the review must come from **Fable 5.1**.

**How to run it (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7, verbatim brief):**
- Post `/review ext/<id> (Fable)` first.
- Spawn a **fresh** Fable sub-agent and give it only the following:
  - the diff;
  - a delimited block holding only this PR's `Closes #102`, `Claim:` and `Author model:` lines;
  - issue #102, which is the spec;
  - AGENTS.md, LESSONS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and HFR-PROTOCOL.md.
- Do **not** pass it the PR body's explanations or the mutation results.
- Head to review: the current head (`e4ae1c6` at the time of writing). Merge `dev-swift` first if the CHANGELOG-LEGACY row conflicts. dev-swift now has rows up to **30** (updated 10:20 UTC, after #313), so this PR's row becomes **31 or later**.
- Focus:
  - every test edits a committed capture in memory (no hand-built page);
  - each test fails when its behaviour regresses;
  - a link without an `href` never yields a path;
  - the CHANGELOG-LEGACY row cites the legacy lines.
- Post the verdict verbatim: `**Adversarial review (Fable, ext/<id>, independent of the author): APPROVE | REQUEST CHANGES** — head <sha>`. On REQUEST CHANGES, fix the High and Medium findings in one commit, and have the same reviewer re-check that head.
- **Merge:** the author has no write access to ezzz/HFRnow. After the APPROVE and green CI, comment `READY FOR REVIEW — merge-ready at <sha>`; the steward merges and closes #102.

